 be training such  as those elbow tendons weak elbow  tendons can lead to injury if you're  trying to do movements like rope  climbing or like planche all the cool  stuff that we want to be able to  incorporate into a real superhero  metahuman training program so you can  incorporate some straight arm positions  such as the crow pose as well as support  holds on the Rings other good moves that  rings turned-out push-ups also on the  gymnastic rings or you can use see you  though planche push-ups whilst on the  calisthenics segment I also recommend  toughening up your fingers which you can  do through a whole range of things I  made a video on that also using a  fingerboard and your grip strength and  in a bit of explosive plyometric work in  there for good measure the last thing  you want to focus on as you build your  foundations for this training is your  work capacity work capacity is your  ability to perform exercise for a long  period of time without burning out the  more you can train without getting tired  to the greater work of volume you can  accomplish and the faster you'll see  that progress and if you look at  Batman's training program the one that  was shared in the Batman files you'll  see that it involves an insane amount of  pure work as you would have to include  if you were trying to train in such a  cross-modal manner there lots of things  you can do to increase work capacity and  again I made a whole video on this in  the past but one of my favorite methods  comes from the world's fittest book by  Ross Edgley and this is called a  workhorse training and this is to  include a cardio finisher at the end of  each workout but to make it a form of  resistance cardio that means that you're  not only exerting yourself in an aerobic  fashion but you're so pushing or pulling  against some form of resistance so  examples might be running up a steep  hill cycling on a tough resistance  setting rowing  seen better yet battle ropes kettlebell  swings heavy bag work anything like that  I guess your heart pumping but still  also targets the muscles and gets them  working too and all of this should help  to get the best start possible and to  train in a manner that goes beyond being  merely functional I personally put all  of this use before day routine that  being push-pull legs you'll be able to  find an example linked in the  description down below over at the bar  near comm search around this video  useful interesting guys if you did then  please leave like please share it around  please subscribe to the channel or if  that helps me out immensely like I say  we're getting close to a hundred  thousand subscribers and when that  happens I've got some really interesting  announcements to make so stay tuned for  that thanks so much for all of your  support and I'll see you in the next one  bye for now

